<%# **A trail needs somewhere to go back to.** On a top-level index this rendered "Dashboard > Classrooms"
    directly above an h1 reading "Classrooms" - the page's own name twice, 30px apart - and its one link
    duplicated the sidebar's own Dashboard item. Reported as pushing the content down for no value, and
    measured: 44px of it, taking the h1 from y=128 to y=172 on a 768px viewport.

    Carbon says it outright ("do not use breadcrumbs when there is only one level"), GOV.UK shows the path
    *above* the current page so a top-level page has none, and Polaris has no trail at all - a single back
    action on pages that have a parent. A record page keeps its trail, because "Dashboard > Students > Sam
    Student" has a Students to return to. %>
<% return if breadcrumbs.size < 2 %>

<nav class="flex mb-6" aria-label="Breadcrumb">
  <%# flex-wrap, not inline-flex. As a single unwrappable line the trail pushed <main> sideways on
      six admin pages - a school year's crumb reads "School name (2024-2025)" and took the page
      130px past the viewport at 375px, which carried the row actions off screen with it. gap-x
      matches the old space-x at one line, and gap-y spaces the wrapped rows. %>
  <ol class="flex flex-wrap items-center gap-x-1 gap-y-1 lg:gap-x-3">
    <li class="inline-flex items-center">
      <%= link_to admin_root_path, class: "inline-flex items-center text-sm font-medium text-slate-700 hover:text-sitf-primary-dark" do %>
        <%= lucide_icon("house", class: "w-4 h-4 mr-2 shrink-0") %>
        Dashboard
      <% end %>
    </li>

    <% breadcrumbs.each_with_index do |crumb, index| %>
      <li>
        <div class="flex items-center">
          <%= lucide_icon("chevron-right", class: "w-3 h-3 text-slate-500 mx-1 shrink-0") %>
          <% if index == breadcrumbs.length - 1 %>
            <span class="ml-1 text-sm font-medium break-words text-slate-500 lg:ml-2">
              <%= crumb[:label] %>
            </span>
          <% else %>
            <%= link_to crumb[:label], crumb[:path], class: "ml-1 text-sm font-medium break-words text-slate-700 hover:text-sitf-primary-dark lg:ml-2" %>
          <% end %>
        </div>
      </li>
    <% end %>
  </ol>
</nav>
